1
00:00:12,040 --> 00:00:34,959
周一的讲座：将是一场专题讲座，内容不在 Artin 教材内，而是更高等的内容， 特别是我在这个课题上做的一些研究，我认为或许能让你们对当今该领域的研究现状有所了解。
Lecture Monday: A special lecture will not be on material in Artin, but on more advanced material,   in particular some research I did on this subject, which I thought maybe would give you an idea of what's going on today in the subject.

2
00:00:34,959 --> 00:00:59,480
之后我们将进行复习课和各种答疑讲座等，为期末考试和温习周做好准备，相关安排会发布在网站上，所以我们现在就不专门安排了。
And then we'll have review and all kinds of lectures, etc., to get ready for the exam and reading period, and that will be posted on the web, so we won't arrange it right now.

3
00:00:59,480 --> 00:01:02,446
好的。那么上次我们讲到哪里了？
Good. So where were we last time?

4
00:01:02,446 --> 00:01:35,879
上次我们确定了代数整数环的所有元素——在数域 $\mathbb{Q}(\sqrt{d})$ 中（其中 $d$ 为无平方因子整数）； 这些代数整数构成一个环，我们记为 $R$。这里有两种可能的情形。
Last time we determined what all the algebraic integers were in the field $\mathbb{Q}(\sqrt{d})$, where $d$ was a square-free integer;   and the algebraic integers formed a ring we'll call $R$, and in the case—there were two possible cases.

5
00:01:35,879 --> 00:01:54,279
其中一种情形总是包含所有整数，加上 $\sqrt{d}$ 的整数倍，而当 $d \equiv 2$ 或 $3 \pmod 4$ 时，你得到的就只有这些。
Well, there was the case where you always contained all integers plus integer multiples of $\sqrt{d}$, and that was all you got when $d$ was congruent to 2 or 3 mod 4.

6
00:01:54,279 --> 00:02:04,000
而在 $d \equiv 1 \pmod 4$ 的情形下，你得到的东西要多一点：你当然得到了整数，得到了 $\sqrt{d}$ 的倍数，
And in the case where the—the $d$ was congruent to 1 mod 4, you got a little more: so you certainly got the integers, you got the multiples of $\sqrt{d}$,

7
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:14,520
但你也得到了 $(1 + \sqrt{d})/2$ 的倍数，当 $d \equiv 1 \pmod 4$ 时。
but you also got the multiples of $(1 + \sqrt{d})/2$ when $d$ was congruent to 1 mod 4.

8
00:02:14,520 --> 00:02:26,840
特别地，代数整数构成一个环， 这个环就是我们从现在起要深入研究的环。
So in particular the algebraic integers form a ring,   and that ring is the ring we're going to study from now on.

9
00:02:26,840 --> 00:02:32,456
现在有一种统一的书写方式，一种非常优美的统一步骤。
Now there's a uniform way of writing this, a nice uniform way of writing it.

10
00:02:32,456 --> 00:02:52,410
换句话说，代数整数环中的元素具有形式$a + b\sqrt{d}$，其中 $a$ 和 $b$ 都是整数， 或者 $a$ 和 $b$ 都是非整数的半整数——它们必须同为整数或同为半整数。
So in other words, the things in the algebraic integers are of the form $a + b\sqrt{d}$, where $a$ and $b$ are integers,   or $a$ and $b$ are half-integers which are not integers—they both have to be either integers or half-integers.

11
00:02:52,410 --> 00:03:04,080
这发生在 $d \equiv 1 \pmod 4$ 时，因为这个数的倍数其 $a$ 和 $b$都是半整数，而不是整数，对吧？
And this occurs when $d$ is congruent to 1 mod 4, because the multiples of this number have $a$ and $b$ both half-integers, neither integers, right?

12
00:03:04,080 --> 00:03:09,933
如果你——好吧，如果你乘以 2，那么 $a$ 和 $b$ 是整数；但如果乘以 3，$a$ 和 $b$ 就是半整数。
If you—well, if you multiply by 2, then $a$ and $b$ are integers, but if you multiply by 3, $a$ and $b$ are half-integers.

13
00:03:09,933 --> 00:03:14,600
所以这就是代数整数集合。
So these are the set of algebraic integers.

14
00:03:14,600 --> 00:03:26,064
现在统一书写它的方法是引入一个新数， 一个能更好描述这个整数环的数：大写 $D$（判别式），它要么是 $4d$，要么是 $d$。
Now the uniform way of writing this is to introduce a new number,   which is a better number for describing this ring of integers: capital $D$, which is either $4d$ or $d$.

15
00:03:26,064 --> 00:03:38,799
当 $d \equiv 1 \pmod 4$ 时取 $d$，而当 $d$ 同余于2 或 $3 \pmod 4$ 时取 $4d$；
This is the case when $d$ is congruent to 1 mod 4, and this is the case when $d$ is congruent to 2 or 3 mod 4,

16
00:03:38,799 --> 00:03:47,480
在那后一种情形下，这里的这个数变为同余于 $0 \pmod 4$。 因此这个大写 $D$ 要么被 4 整除，要么模 4 余 1。
in which case this number here becomes congruent to 0 mod 4.   So this capital $D$ is either divisible by 4 or has remainder 1 mod 4.

17
00:03:47,480 --> 00:03:54,160
引入它之后，就有了书写该代数整数环的统一方法。
And then if you introduce that, there's a uniform way of writing down this ring of algebraic integers.

18
00:03:54,160 --> 00:04:05,080
你可以把它写成这样——这是一种很巧妙的表示方法：它由 1 的所有倍数以及 $(D + \sqrt{D})/2$ 的所有倍数构成。
You can write it like this—this is a cute way of doing it: it's all multiples of 1 and all multiples of $(D + \sqrt{D})/2$.

19
00:04:05,080 --> 00:04:19,480
为什么会这样呢？因为首先，$\sqrt{D}$ 要么等于 $2\sqrt{d}$，要么等于 $\sqrt{d}$，取决于具体情形。
Now why is that? Because first of all, the square root of $D$ is either equal to $2\sqrt{d}$ or $\sqrt{d}$, depending on what happens.

20
00:04:19,480 --> 00:04:36,200
那么在 $d \equiv 1 \pmod 4$ 的情形下，这正是 $(d + \sqrt{d})/2$；但小写 $d$ 是奇数，所以你可以从中减去一个整数得到这个数， 反之，如果你已知那个数，也可以加上一个整数得到这个数。
So in the case where $d$ is congruent to 1 mod 4, this is $(d + \sqrt{d})/2$, but little $d$ is odd, so you can subtract an integer from it and get this number,   and conversely if you had this number, you could add an integer to it and get that number.

21
00:04:36,200 --> 00:04:42,280
所以当大写 $D$ 为奇数时，这个环与原环完全相同。
So this ring is the same as this ring when capital $D$ is odd.

22
00:04:42,280 --> 00:04:51,151
若大写 $D$ 能被 4 整除，则 $\sqrt{D} = 2\sqrt{d}$，此时分子中的两项都能被 2 整除。
If capital $D$ is divisible by 4, so $\sqrt{D} = 2\sqrt{d}$, then both this number and this number are divisible by 2.

23
00:04:51,151 --> 00:05:00,040
约去 2 后，你就剩下一个整数加上$\sqrt{d}$ 的倍数，因此可以互相表示。
You can divide the 2 out, and you're left with an integer plus a multiple of $\sqrt{d}$, so you can express $\sqrt{d}$ and vice versa.

24
00:05:00,040 --> 00:05:17,160
因此这就是描述代数整数环的统一方法，我们可以把这个环记为 $R_D$ 之类。 这就是为什么我说用大写 $D$ 来作为指标比用小写 $d$ 更方便。
So this is the uniform way of describing the ring of algebraic integers, and we could call this $R_D$ or something like that.   That's why I say it's easier to index by this capital $D$ than it is by the little $d$.

25
00:05:17,160 --> 00:05:34,560
例如，现在我们要特别研究 $D < 0$ 的情形： 它们被称为虚二次环。
So for example, now we're going to study these in particular when $D$ is negative:   they're called imaginary quadratic rings.

26
00:05:35,960 --> 00:05:41,800
在本讲一开始我们就会立刻看到， 为什么这比负——比正判别式的情形要容易得多。
And we're going to see right away at the beginning of this lecture   why this is an easier case than the negative—than the positive.

27
00:05:41,800 --> 00:05:57,814
如果像我上次那样列出所有小于 0 的 $D$ 的可能取值， 它们依次是 $-3, -4, -7, -8,$$-11$（$-12$ 不行）、
And if you list out the possibilities for $D$ that are less than 0, as I did last time,   they look like $-3, -4, -7, -8,$ $-11$ ($-12$ is no good),

28
00:05:57,814 --> 00:06:09,125
$-15$（$-16$ 不行）、$-19, -20, -23$ 等等。 因此这里有非常多的由这些指标标记的有趣环。
$-15$ ($-16$ is), $-19, -20, -23$, etc.   So there are an awful lot of interesting rings indexed by this.

29
00:06:09,125 --> 00:06:16,680
这里的这一项 $D = -4$ 对应于 $d = -1$，那就是高斯整数环。
And this case here, this $D = -4$, is where $d = -1$, and that's the Gaussian integers.

30
00:06:16,680 --> 00:06:25,480
这是我们已经研究过的情形； 而所有其他情形都是全新的环，它们对我们来说非常值得探讨。
So that's the case we've looked at,   and all these other cases are new rings that are going to be interesting for us to study.

31
00:06:25,480 --> 00:06:38,481
大家都看明白了吗：仅凭选取一个整数并定义这样一个环， 你就得到了一个有趣的环，它可能具有也可能不具有唯一因子分解，这正是我们要研究的。
So does everyone see how just taking an integer, defining a ring like this,   you get an interesting ring which may or may not have unique factorization, which we're going to want to study?

32
00:06:38,481 --> 00:06:51,022
好的。现在首先要向大家展示的是， 为什么这种情形比正数情形（称为实二次环）要容易得多：让我们观察一下存在如下映射。
Okay. Now the first thing to show you   why this case is easier than the positive case, which are called real quadratic rings: let's just observe that we have the following map.

33
00:06:51,022 --> 00:07:06,427
我断言存在一个映射 $\Delta$，Artin 称之为范数映射（也是其常用记号），在所有这些情形下它都从环 $R$ 映到整数环 $\mathbb{Z}$。
I claim we have a map $\Delta$, which Artin calls the norm map—that's the usual notation for it— from the ring $R$ to the ring $\mathbb{Z}$ in any of these cases.

34
00:07:06,427 --> 00:07:23,719
映射形式如下：它将形如$a + b\sqrt{d}$ 的元素映为它的范数：$a^2 - db^2$。
And the map looks like this: it takes something of the form $a + b\sqrt{d}$ and if I want to take the norm of it, I take it to $a^2 - d b^2$.

35
00:07:23,719 --> 00:07:40,839
换句话说，这正是这个数 $a + b\sqrt{d}$ 与另一个数 $a - b\sqrt{d}$ 的乘积。 如果前一个元素记作 $\alpha$，那么后一个环中元素记作 $\alpha'$。
In other words, that's the product of this number $a + b\sqrt{d}$ with the other number $a - b\sqrt{d}$.   If this thing is called $\alpha$, then this number in the ring is called $\alpha'$.

36
00:07:40,839 --> 00:07:46,782
存在一个从该环到自身的自同构，将这个数映为某种意义上的共轭。
There's a way of taking the ring to itself which takes this number to, in some sense, its conjugate.

37
00:07:46,782 --> 00:07:56,437
如果你在环中将这两个数相乘，会注意到 $\sqrt{d}$ 前面的交叉项抵消了， 因为你有一项带负号的 $-ab\sqrt{d}$，
And if you multiply these two numbers in the ring, notice that the terms before $\sqrt{d}$ go away,   because you have $-ab\sqrt{d}$,

38
00:07:56,437 --> 00:08:03,960
而这里有一项带正号的 $+ab\sqrt{d}$，所以你只得到一个普通的数。 现在我断言该数是一个整数。
but here you have $ab\sqrt{d}$ with a plus sign, so you just get a normal number.   Now I claim that number is an integer.

39
00:08:03,960 --> 00:08:17,030
这并不是显然成立的： 当 $a$ 和 $b$ 都是整数时显然成立，但当 $a$ 和 $b$都是半整数时你必须验证它也是整数。
That's not completely obvious:   it's completely obvious in this case when $a$ and $b$ are both integers, but you have to check that it's an integer when $a$ and $b$ are both half-integers.

40
00:08:17,030 --> 00:08:24,200
不过若 $a, b$ 都是半整数，由 $d \equiv 1 \pmod 4$ 的事实，意味着这个数最终确实是一个整数。
But if $a$ and $b$ are both half-integers, then the fact that $d$ is 1 mod 4 means that this number turns out to be an integer.

41
00:08:24,200 --> 00:08:35,000
我的意思是，先验地看它是某个整数的四分之一，但你检查一下就会发现：$a^2 \equiv 1 \pmod 4$，且 $b^2$ 同余…… 所以你会发现这个数最终确实是一个整数。
I mean, a priori it's 1/4 of an integer, but you—you'll check, you see that $a^2$ is congruent to 1 mod 4, and $b^2$ is congruent...   So you'll see that this number turns out to be an integer.

42
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:45,948
特别地，数 $a + b\sqrt{d}$ 与另一个数相乘的积是一个真正的整数。
So in particular, this product of the number $a + b\sqrt{d}$ times this other number is an actual integer.

43
00:08:45,948 --> 00:08:58,674
并且这个将二次环的元素映到普通整数环的映射， 具有优良的性质：乘积的范数等于范数的乘积。
And this map, which takes elements of our quadratic ring to elements in the normal ring,   has the nice property that if you take the norm of a product, it's the product of the norms.

44
00:08:58,674 --> 00:09:07,800
我们在高斯数中见过这一点。 原因是乘积的范数就是 $\alpha\alpha'$乘 $\beta\beta'$。
We saw this in the Gaussian numbers.   And the reason is that this norm of a product is just $\alpha \alpha'$ times $\beta \beta'$.

45
00:09:07,800 --> 00:09:25,576
好吧，严格说是 $(\alpha\beta)(\alpha\beta)'$， 你会发现 $(\alpha\beta)' = \alpha'\beta'$，然后重排各项，
Well, really, sorry, it's $(\alpha\beta)(\alpha\beta)'$,   and you find that $(\alpha\beta)'$ is $\alpha' \beta'$, and then you rearrange it, and then you rewrite it

46
00:09:25,576 --> 00:09:34,840
将其改写为 $(\alpha\alpha')(\beta\beta')$， 这里利用了该环中乘法的交换性，于是你认出这正是 $\alpha$ 的范数乘上 $\beta$ 的范数。
as $(\alpha\alpha')(\beta\beta')$,   using the fact that multiplication is commutative in this ring, and then you recognize this is the norm of $\alpha$ and this is the norm of $\beta$.

47
00:09:34,840 --> 00:09:51,400
所以它是可乘的：它不是可加的，但至少是可乘的。 好的，这能让我们像在高斯数中那样确定环中的单位元是什么。
So it's multiplicative: it's not additive, but at least it's multiplicative.   Okay, so this will allow us to identify, as we did in the Gaussian numbers, what the units of the ring are.

48
00:09:51,400 --> 00:10:06,720
啊，还有一个观察， 这正是为什么对于 $D < 0$，条件会如此好——这正是其性质极佳的原因：查看范数，它是一个整数， 但当我们处于虚二次情形时，
Ah, one more observation,   and this is the reason that for $D < 0$, this is the reason that this condition becomes so nice: if you look at the norms, this is an integer,   but when we're in the imaginary quadratic case,

49
00:10:06,720 --> 00:10:21,319
它是一个非负整数，因为这一项是平方，这一项也是平方，而且这里有 $-d$（$d < 0$）， 所以我们取的是两个正数的和。
it's a non-negative integer, because this is a square, this is a square, and we have a $-d$ here,   so we're taking the sum of positive numbers.

50
00:10:21,319 --> 00:10:37,480
这就是让虚二次情形容易得多的本质原因：范数是非负的。 现在我断言，关于单位元有如下结论，且这在所有情形下都成立。
So this really makes the imaginary quadratic case so much easier: the norm is non-negative.   Now I claim we have the following result on units, and this is true in all cases.

51
00:10:37,480 --> 00:11:03,493
命题：$\alpha$ 是环 $R$ 中的单位元，当且仅当 $\alpha$ 的范数（即 $\pm 1$）是 $\mathbb{Z}$ 中的单位。
Proposition: $\alpha$ is a unit in $R$—sorry, in the ring $R$—if and only if the norm of $\alpha$, which is $\pm 1$, is a unit in $\mathbb{Z}$.   Okay, so that you can test whether

52
00:11:03,493 --> 00:11:12,639
好的，因此你可以通过计算该整数并观察它在整数环中是否可逆，来检验该元素在环中是否可逆。
this thing is invertible in the ring by calculating this integer and seeing whether it's invertible in the integers.

53
00:11:12,639 --> 00:11:25,800
证明：若 $\alpha$ 是单位，则环中存在 $\beta$ 满足 $\alpha\beta = 1$。
Proof: If $\alpha$ is a unit, there exists a $\beta$ in the ring where $\alpha \beta = 1$.

54
00:11:25,800 --> 00:11:40,826
这就是单位的定义。两边取范数： 则 $\alpha\beta$ 的范数即 $\alpha$ 的范数乘 $\beta$ 的范数，等于 1 的范数。
That's what a unit means. Apply the norm:   then the norm of $\alpha\beta$, which is the norm of $\alpha$ times the norm of $\beta$, is the norm of 1.

55
00:11:40,826 --> 00:11:48,600
但 1 的范数就是 1， 因为 $b = 0$ 且 $a = 1$。
But the norm of 1 is just 1,   because $b = 0$ and $a = 1$.

56
00:11:48,600 --> 00:12:00,759
于是这是两个乘积为 1 的整数。 因此 $\alpha$ 的范数必须是整数环中的单位，从而整数环中仅有的单位是 $\pm 1$。
So here are two integers whose product is 1.   Therefore the norm of $\alpha$ has to be a unit in the integers, and consequently the only units in the integers are $\pm 1$.

57
00:12:00,759 --> 00:12:19,353
反之，若 $\alpha$ 的范数（即 $\alpha\alpha'$）等于 $\pm 1$，则 $\pm\alpha'$ 就是 $\alpha$ 的逆元。
Conversely, if the norm of $\alpha$ (which remember is $\alpha \alpha'$) is equal to $\pm 1$, then $\pm \alpha'$ is an inverse for $\alpha$.

58
00:12:19,353 --> 00:12:34,120
并且该元素也在环中，因为如果 $a + b\sqrt{d}$在环中，那么 $a$ 和 $b$ 同为整数或同为半整数； 从而共轭项也同为整数或半整数，所以在环中。
And this element is in the ring too, because if $a + b\sqrt{d}$ is in the ring, then $a$ and $b$ are both integers or half-integers;   consequently these are both integers or half-integers, so this is in the ring.

59
00:12:34,120 --> 00:12:45,240
这就给出了逆元，因为拿它相乘： 要么得到 $+1$，此时 $\alpha'$ 是逆元；要么得到 $-1$，此时 $-\alpha'$ 是逆元。
And that gives you the inverse, because here's a thing that you multiply it by:   you either get $+1$, in which case $\alpha'$ is an inverse, or you get $-1$, in which case $-\alpha'$ is an inverse.

60
00:12:45,240 --> 00:13:13,040
好的。因此推论：若 $D < 0$，则 $\alpha$ 是单位元 当且仅当 $\alpha$ 的范数为 $+1$，因为在那类情形中我们看到范数全是非负的，所以不可能是 $-1$。
Okay. Thus, corollary: if $D < 0$, then $\alpha$ is a unit   if and only if the norm of $\alpha$ is $+1$, because in that case we saw the norms are all non-negative, so it can't be $-1$.

61
00:13:13,040 --> 00:13:46,439
好的，现在我们来列举负判别式情形下的所有单位元。事实上，若 $D = -3$，有 6 个单位元； 若 $D = -4$，有 4 个单位元；而当 $D < -4$ 时，只有 2 个单位元。
All right, now let's enumerate the units in the negative case. In fact, if $D = -3$, there are 6 units;   if $D = -4$, there are 4 units; and if $D < -4$, there are 2 units.

62
00:13:46,439 --> 00:13:51,949
实际上在这些情形下，单位群与整数环的单位群相同， 仅仅是 $\pm 1$。
In fact, in this case the unit group is the same as the unit group of $\mathbb{Z}$,   just $\pm 1$.

63
00:13:51,949 --> 00:14:07,240
所以对于几乎所有这些情形（除前两种外），你在环中都得不到任何未知的全新单位元： 除了当 $a = \pm 1$且 $b = 0$ 之外，没有其他元素可逆。
So for almost all these cases, except for the first two, you don't get any new units in the ring that you didn't know about:   nothing is invertible except when $a$ is equal to $\pm 1$ and $b = 0$.

64
00:14:07,240 --> 00:14:14,680
好的，我们来证明它。我们在寻找方程的解。
All right, let's prove it. Well, we're looking for solutions.

65
00:14:14,680 --> 00:14:41,360
证明：单位元 $\alpha = a + b\sqrt{d}$ 是方程 $a^2 - d b^2 = 1$ 的解，其中 $a$ 和 $b$ 要么都是整数，要么都是半整数。
Proof: A unit $\alpha = a + b\sqrt{d}$ is a solution to $a^2 - d b^2 = 1$, where $a$ and $b$ are either integers, or they're half-integers.

66
00:14:42,600 --> 00:15:13,480
好，现在看这里：如果 $b = 0$，对吧， 那么 $a^2$ 必须等于 1，所以 $a = \pm 1$，这就得到了 $\mathbb{Z}^\times$ 中的单位元， 即我们早已熟知的那些元素。
Okay, now look at this: if $b = 0$, right,   then $a^2$ has to be 1, so $a = \pm 1$, and there you get the units in $\mathbb{Z}^\times$,   those things we already knew about.

67
00:15:13,480 --> 00:15:34,267
如果 $b \ne 0$（不好意思）， 那么 $-b^2 d$大于或等于 $-D/4$，对吧？
If $b \ne 0$, I'm sorry,   then $-b^2 d$ is greater than or equal to $-D/4$, right?

68
00:15:34,267 --> 00:15:54,366
因为无论 $b$ 取何值，$b$ 的绝对值都至少为 $1/2$，所以 $b^2 \ge 1/4$，因此该项至少是 $-D/4$。 因为 $b$ 必须是半整数，所以这至少是 $-D/4$。
Because whatever $b$ is, $|b| \ge 1/2$, so $b^2 \ge 1/4$, so it's $-D/4$, how about that?   Because $b$ has got to be a half-integer, so this has got to be $-D/4$.

69
00:15:54,366 --> 00:16:13,342
一旦 $-D$ 大于——如果，如果如果$-D > 4$，就绝无可能了，对吧？
Once $-D$ is bigger than—if, if if $-D > 4$, it's hopeless, right?

70
00:16:13,342 --> 00:16:22,575
因为那样该数就会大于 1， 这两项绝不可能相加等于 1——各项都是正的，对吧？
Because then this number will be bigger than 1,   and there's no way that these things can add up to 1—this number is positive, right?

71
00:16:22,575 --> 00:16:31,319
所以这排除了几乎所有情况，然后只需检查这两种情形，便能得到有限个解。
So that eliminates almost everything, and then you just check these two cases and you find the various solutions—a finite number.

72
00:16:31,319 --> 00:16:42,791
另一方面，看看当$D$ 为正时会发生什么：若 $D > 0$， 这就是一个平方与平方倍数的差，对吧？
On the other hand, look at what happens if $D$ is positive: if $D$ is positive,   this is the difference of a square and some multiple of a square, right?

73
00:16:42,791 --> 00:16:54,480
所以你完全可以设想无论 $a$ 和 $b$ 有多大，差值都可能为 1。 我是说，它们不是相加：而是一个平方减去 $d$ 乘平方。
So you could certainly imagine that difference being 1 no matter how big $a$ and $b$ are.   I mean, they're not adding up: you're taking a square minus $d$ times a square.

74
00:16:54,480 --> 00:17:00,920
事实上可以证明，若 $D > 0$，总存在无限多个单位元。
And in fact, it turns out that if $D$ is positive, there are always an infinite number of units.

75
00:17:00,920 --> 00:17:12,759
事实上——虽然我不打算在此证明——若$D > 0$，则 $R^\times$ 是无限群，这会带来很多麻烦。
In fact—which I'm not going to prove—if $D > 0$, $R^\times$ is infinite, and that gives a lot of headache.

76
00:17:12,759 --> 00:17:40,067
我给你们举个例子，第一个简单的例子：例：$d = 5$。这是最小的正无平方因子数 $d$。 那里 $R = \mathbb{Z} + \mathbb{Z} \frac{1 + \sqrt{5}}{2}$。
I'll give you an example, this first simple example: Example: $d = 5$. That's the smallest positive $d$.   So there $R = \mathbb{Z} + \mathbb{Z} \frac{1 + \sqrt{5}}{2}$.

77
00:17:40,067 --> 00:17:50,599
现在令 $\alpha = (1 + \sqrt{5})/2$。 这是数学史上的一个著名常数，称为黄金分割。
Now let $\alpha$ be the number $(1 + \sqrt{5})/2$.   This is a famous number in the history of math called the golden mean.

78
00:17:50,599 --> 00:18:03,448
如果你构造一个矩形，使得切去一个正方形后得到相似的矩形，那么边长之比就是它。
Okay, it's the—if you build a rectangle such that when you chop off a square you get a similar rectangle, then the ratio of the sides is that.

79
00:18:03,448 --> 00:18:13,720
帕特农神庙（对那些假期回希腊的人来说）的尺寸就是黄金比例。所有古典建筑都建立在黄金分割之上。
The Parthenon, for those returning to Greece for the holidays, has dimensions of the golden mean. All classical architecture was built on the golden mean.

80
00:18:13,720 --> 00:18:22,666
20 世纪著名建筑大师勒·柯布西耶设计了木工中心（你们中许多人可能在那里上过绘画课），他认为不应该给建筑师发尺子，
Le Corbusier, one of the great 20th-century architects who designed the Carpenter Center, where many of you may have taken drawing classes, believed that architects should not be given rulers:

81
00:18:22,666 --> 00:18:35,000
只应该发一根标有 1 和黄金分割长度的木棍，一切都应依此设计！ 无论如何，这里的 $\alpha = (1 + \sqrt{5})/2$。
they should just be given a stick on which was marked out 1 and the length of the golden mean—everything should be designed according to that!   Anyhow, here is this $\alpha = (1 + \sqrt{5})/2$.

82
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:51,719
现在如果将 $\alpha \alpha'$ 相乘，得到 $\frac{1 + \sqrt{5}}{2} \cdot \frac{1 - \sqrt{5}}{2}$，即 $(1^2 - 5)/4 = -1$。
Now if you multiply $\alpha \alpha'$, you get $\frac{1 + \sqrt{5}}{2} \cdot \frac{1 - \sqrt{5}}{2}$, which is $(1^2 - 5)/4$, which is $-1$.

83
00:18:51,719 --> 00:19:01,760
这由上面的命题表明， $\alpha$ 是一个单位元，其逆元为 $-\alpha'$。
So that shows, by our proposition up here,   that $\alpha$ is a unit with inverse $-\alpha'$.

84
00:19:04,680 --> 00:19:07,719
好的，这是一个单位元。
Okay, so here's one unit.

85
00:19:07,719 --> 00:19:18,839
要找到无穷多个单位元，我们计算 $\alpha^2$：$\alpha^2$ 算出来是 $(3 + \sqrt{5})/2$。
To find an infinite number of units, you calculate $\alpha^2$: so $\alpha^2$ turns out to be $(3 + \sqrt{5})/2$.

86
00:19:18,839 --> 00:19:28,359
好，如果乘开，会得到 $(6 + 2\sqrt{5})/4$， 约分后就得到这个式子。
Okay, if you multiply, you get $(6 + 2\sqrt{5})/4$,   and then you divide out, you get this.

87
00:19:28,359 --> 00:19:42,760
所以这也是一个单位元，因为 $\Delta$ 是可乘的。 我们发现 $\Delta(\alpha) = -1$ 意味着 $\Delta(\alpha^2)$为 $+1$，因此是另一个单位元。
So this is also a unit, because $\Delta$ is multiplicative.   So we find that $\Delta(\alpha) = -1$ implies $\Delta(\alpha^2)$ is $+1$, so that's another unit.

88
00:19:42,760 --> 00:20:02,040
好的，然后取 $\alpha^3$，得到又一个单位元。 算算看是什么：$9 + 5 = 14$，所以是 $(7 + 3\sqrt{5})/2$。那是又一个单位元，范数为 $-1$。
Okay, then you take $\alpha^3$, you get another unit.   Let's see what it is: $9 + 5$, that's 14, so it's $(7 + 3\sqrt{5})/2$. That's another unit, that one has norm $-1$.

89
00:20:02,040 --> 00:20:07,640
你继续取 $\alpha$ 的更高次幂，永远不会回到 1——事实上，各项系数 $a$ 和 $b$ 会越来越大。
And you keep taking powers of $\alpha$, you never get back to 1—in fact, the $a$'s and $b$'s keep getting bigger and bigger.

90
00:20:07,640 --> 00:20:25,423
这是单位元，因为 $7^2 = 49$ 减去 $9 \times 5 = 45$ 等于 4， 或者 $-4$——我哪里算错了吗？
So this is a unit because $7^2 = 49$, minus $9 \times 5 = 45$, is equal to 4,   or maybe $-4$—what did I do wrong there?

91
00:20:25,423 --> 00:20:29,940
这个范数怎么会是 $-1$ 呢？
How can this norm be $-1$?

92
00:20:29,940 --> 00:20:39,757
对，$\alpha^3$ 的范数是 $-1$， 但我是说，这——这是因为它是等于 1 的近似解——事实上这算出来是 4。
Yeah, the norm of $\alpha^3$ is $-1$,   but I mean, it's—it's the fact that you have an approximate solution to this equal to 1—in fact, this turns out to be 4.

93
00:20:39,757 --> 00:20:50,006
好的。所以这里得到了无限多个单位元：$\alpha^n$ 互不相同。
Okay. So here you get an infinite number of units: $\alpha^n$ are all distinct.

94
00:20:50,680 --> 00:21:02,920
事实上，这个群是无限群这一事实与数学中著名的经典结果——佩尔方程（Pell's equation）的求解密切相关， 欧拉曾利用连分数理论彻底解决了该问题。
And in fact, the fact that this group is infinite is related to a famous classical result in mathematics called the solution of Pell's equation,   which Euler worked out using the theory of continued fractions.

95
00:21:02,920 --> 00:21:07,320
我们不对此展开讨论——那是非常有趣的课题，大家可以在 Artin 书中阅读更多内容。
We're not going to go there—that's a really interesting subject, you can read about it more in Artin.

96
00:21:07,320 --> 00:21:12,235
但在这里我们仅专注于负判别式的数域，其单位群是有限的。
But here we're just going to concentrate on these fields with negative discriminant, where the unit group is finite.

97
00:21:12,235 --> 00:21:22,559
事实上，其单位群几乎总是等于整数环的单位群，并且我们接下来要进一步研究理想理论。
In fact, the unit group is almost always just the unit group of the integers, and we're going to go on to study a little bit more of the ideal theory.

98
00:21:28,640 --> 00:21:54,920
好的。现在你可能会说：“这研究得太冷僻了吧，我们为什么要搞这个无聊环的理想理论？” 原因在于，这正是“理想”概念最初被发现的地方。
Okay. Now you might say, "Well, this is getting awfully specialized. Why are we doing the ideal theory of this silly ring?"   And the reason is, this is where ideals were discovered.

99
00:21:54,920 --> 00:22:08,200
建立抽象环论以及理想、主理想的抽象理论固然很好， 但这里正是数学家们最早不得不面对“非主理想存在”这一客观事实， 并想出应对办法的历史发源地。
It's all very nice to have an abstract theory of rings, and an abstract theory of ideals, principal ideals, etc.,   but this is the place where people first came to grapple with the fact that there were non-principal ideals,   and figured out what to do about it.

100
00:22:08,200 --> 00:22:16,240
因此回顾孕育出整个理论的原初问题通常大有裨益。
So it's often nice to look at the original problem from which the entire theory arose.

101
00:22:16,240 --> 00:22:33,760
好的，我们之前看到当 $d$ 等于呃——抱歉，当 $d = -1$ 时，我们得到了高斯整数环，它是一个欧几里得环。
All right, now we saw that when $d$ was equal to uh— sorry, when $d = -1$, so we got the Gaussian integers, it is a Euclidean ring.

102
00:22:36,599 --> 00:22:53,760
然而我断言：若 $d \equiv 3 \pmod 4$ 且 $d < -1$—— 即对于所有其他 $d$ 模 4 余 3的负数情形—
However, I claim that if $d \equiv 3 \pmod 4$ and $d < -1$—   namely for all the other negative cases where $d$ is congruent to 3 mod 4—

103
00:22:53,760 --> 00:23:09,800
—我断言 $R = \mathbb{Z} + \mathbb{Z}\sqrt{d}$ 决不是唯一分解整环（UFD）。
I claim then $R$, which is $\mathbb{Z} + \mathbb{Z}\sqrt{d}$, is not a unique factorization domain.

104
00:23:09,800 --> 00:23:26,993
例如我们在 $d = -5$ 时就见过了，但它对 $-13$ 也成立，对 $-17$ 也成立，对$-21$ 等也成立。
For example, we saw this for $d = -5$, but it's also true for $-13$, and it's also true for $-17$, and it's also true for $-21$, etc.

105
00:23:26,993 --> 00:23:36,120
因此对于这无穷多种情形，分解都不唯一。 所以这是一个截然不同的典型非 UFD 结果。
So for all that infinite number of these, we're going to get non-unique factorization.   So this is a completely atypical result.

106
00:23:36,120 --> 00:23:46,129
请记住，我们在高斯整数中用到了：若 $a, b \le 1/2$，则 $a^2 + b^2$ 严格小于1。
And remember, we used the fact that $a^2 + b^2$ was somehow—if $a$ and $b$ were both less than a half, $a^2 + b^2$ was less than 1.

107
00:23:46,129 --> 00:23:55,000
但在这里我们将遇到形如 $a^2 - db^2$ 的式子， 它不会小于1。
But here we're going to have things like $a^2 - d b^2$,   and that's not going to be less than 1.

108
00:23:55,000 --> 00:24:04,866
为了向你们说明这一点，我必须给出一个元素的两种不同因数分解， 并向你们证明这些因子都是素元，对吧？
So to show you this, I have to give you a factorization of something in two different ways,   and show you that the factors are prime elements, right?

109
00:24:04,866 --> 00:24:31,997
因此请看下面的因数分解：考虑 $1 - d$。我要用两种不同方式来分解 $1 - d$： 我将其写成 $(1 + \sqrt{d})(1 - \sqrt{d})$，同时我也将其写成 $2 \cdot \frac{1 - d}{2}$。
So consider the factorization of $1 - d$. So I'm going to write $1 - d$ in two different ways:   I'm going to write it as $(1 + \sqrt{d}) (1 - \sqrt{d})$, and I'm going to write it as $2 \cdot \frac{1 - d}{2}$.

110
00:24:31,997 --> 00:24:40,280
由于 $d \equiv 3 \pmod 4$，它是一个奇数，所以用 1 减去它就会得到一个偶数。
Now since $d \equiv 3 \pmod 4$, it's an odd number, so if I subtract it from 1, I get an even number.

111
00:24:40,280 --> 00:24:48,520
所以这是整数，这也是整数——它们都在我们的环中， 而且这些显然也是我们环里的元素。
So this is an integer, this is an integer—those are elements in our ring,   and these are certainly elements in our ring.

112
00:24:48,520 --> 00:25:08,440
好的，所以我断言：2 是 $R$ 中的一个不可约元——数字 2。
Okay, so I claim: 2 is an irreducible element in $R$—the number 2.

113
00:25:08,440 --> 00:25:12,680
所以在该环中你无法以任何本质方式对 2 进行因数分解。
So you can't factor 2 in any essential way in this ring.

114
00:25:12,680 --> 00:25:26,731
但在那个欧几里得环（高斯整数）中并非如此：你可以分解 2： $2 = (1 + i)(1 - i)$，且两者都不是单位元。
Now that was false in this Euclidean ring: you could factor 2:   $2 = (1 + i)(1 - i)$, and neither of these were units.

115
00:25:26,731 --> 00:25:30,240
但在我们这些环中无法分解 2。 证明：为什么？
But in these rings, I can't factor 2.   Proof: Why?

116
00:25:30,240 --> 00:26:03,058
假设 $2 = \alpha\beta$，其中$\alpha$ 和 $\beta$ 都不是单位。那么取范数：2 的范数等于 4， 它等于 $\alpha$ 的范数乘 $\beta$ 的范数，因为范数是可乘的。
Suppose $2 = \alpha\beta$, with neither $\alpha$ nor $\beta$ a unit. Then take the norm: the norm of 2, which is equal to 4,   is equal to the norm of $\alpha$ times the norm of $\beta$, because the norm is multiplicative.

117
00:26:03,058 --> 00:26:08,640
所以我们对该环的大量研究都将借助范数将其转化为普通整数的性质。
So a lot of our study of this ring is going to be using the norm to turn it into a property of the integers.

118
00:26:08,640 --> 00:26:16,200
现在若 $\alpha$ 和 $\beta$ 不是单位元，它们的范数满足什么？
Now if $\alpha$ and $\beta$ are not units, what do we know about their norms?

119
00:26:16,200 --> 00:26:20,680
不等于 $\pm 1$，或者在这里不等于 $+1$，因为范数是正的。
Not equal to $\pm 1$, or in this case not equal to $+1$, because the norm is positive.

120
00:26:20,680 --> 00:26:30,200
因此这里将 4 写成了两个均不为 1 的整数之积。 这对 $\alpha$ 和 $\beta$ 的范数说明了什么？它们必须都等于 2！
So here we have 4 written as the product of two integers neither of which is 1.   What does that tell us about the norms of $\alpha$ and $\beta$?

121
00:26:30,200 --> 00:26:51,143
因此，如果在该环中存在分解，我们就会找到 范数为 2 的元素。
Therefore, we would have found in this ring, if we had a factorization,   elements of norm 2.

122
00:26:51,143 --> 00:26:58,280
这在高斯整数中是没问题的：那些元素确实具有范数 2—— 这是元素 $\alpha$，这是元素 $\beta$，二者的范数都是 2。
Now that's okay in that ring: these elements do have norm 2—   here's the element $\alpha$, here's the element $\beta$, both of them have norm 2.

123
00:26:58,280 --> 00:27:16,750
好，但在这里这是不可能的：我们将 $\alpha$ 写成 $a + b\sqrt{d}$， 在这种情形下我们知道 $a$ 和 $b$ 都是整数，对吧？
All right, but here this is impossible: we write $\alpha = a + b\sqrt{d}$,   where in this case we know $a$ and $b$ are integers, right?

124
00:27:16,750 --> 00:27:26,512
因为我们处于 $d \equiv 3 \pmod 4$ 的情形，整数环就是它。 怎么了，Tim？请再说一遍？
Because we're in a case where $d \equiv 3 \pmod 4$, so the ring of integers is just this.   Yeah, Tim? Pardon?

125
00:27:26,512 --> 00:27:45,320
不，因为请记住在虚二次环中，$\alpha$ 的范数总是 $\ge 0$： 它等于 $a^2 - db^2$，$a^2$ 与 $b^2$ 为正且 $d$ 为负，所以该数大于等于 0，懂了吗？
No, because remember in an imaginary quadratic ring, the norm of $\alpha$ is always $\ge 0$:   it's $a^2 - d b^2$, $a^2$ and $b^2$ are positive and $d$ is negative, so this number is $\ge 0$, okay?

126
00:27:45,320 --> 00:27:57,880
所以在讨论一般单位元时，实二次可能有 $-1$， 但在虚二次中范数总是正的，这就是为什么范数不必是 $\pm 2$，在这里必须确确实实是 2。
So in general when we're doing units, we had the possibility of $-1$ for real quadratic,   but in the imaginary quadratic the norm is always positive, so that's why they don't have to be $\pm 2$, they really have to be 2 here.

127
00:27:57,880 --> 00:28:09,000
好的，现在这是不可能的，因为若把 $\alpha$ 写成这样，$\alpha$ 的范数就是 $a^2 - db^2$。
Okay, now this is impossible, because if we write $\alpha$ like this, the norm of $\alpha$ is $a^2 - d b^2$.

128
00:28:09,000 --> 00:28:14,280
现在这怎么可能等于 2 呢？
Now how could this possibly be equal to 2?

129
00:28:14,280 --> 00:28:33,079
我是说，这个数相当大：一旦 $-d \ge 5$，该数至少是 $5b^2$ 或 $13b^2$， 绝不可能等于 2。
I mean, this number is quite large: once $-d \ge 5$, this number would be at least $5 b^2$, or $13 b^2$,   so there's no way that could be equal to 2.

130
00:28:33,079 --> 00:28:42,839
因此这迫使 $b = 0$， 因为在我们的列表中$-d \ge 5$。
So this would imply $b = 0$,   as $-d \ge 5$ on our list.

131
00:28:42,839 --> 00:28:50,199
既然 $b = 0$，这就推出 $a^2 = 2$， 这是矛盾，因为 2 不是完全平方数！
And since $b = 0$, that would imply $a^2 = 2$,   which is a contradiction because 2 isn't a square!

132
00:28:50,199 --> 00:28:56,178
现在你再次看到，这在实二次情形下将极难检验。
Now you see again, this would be very, very difficult to check in the real quadratic case.

133
00:28:56,178 --> 00:29:04,760
我是说，实二次中完全可能出现非常大的 $a$ 和非常大的 $b$ 使得该式等于 2： 这项极其庞大，这项也极其庞大，而两者的差可以是 2。
I mean, it's certainly possible you could have a very big $a$ and a very big $b$ such that this thing could equal 2:   this could be huge, this could be huge, and their difference could be 2.

134
00:29:04,760 --> 00:29:08,760
但若两项均为正，相加绝不可能等于 2！
But they can't add up to 2 if they're both positive!

135
00:29:08,760 --> 00:29:14,839
好的，因此我们导出了矛盾，所以 2 不能以这种方式分解。
Okay, so therefore we get a contradiction, and therefore 2 could not factor this way.

136
00:29:14,839 --> 00:29:28,920
因此 2 是一个不可约元。 下面说明为什么它不是唯一分解整环：2 整除 $1 - d$，因为这里有它的因式分解。
So therefore 2 is an irreducible element.   Now here's why we can't have a unique factorization domain: 2 divides $1 - d$, because here's a factorization of it.

137
00:29:28,920 --> 00:29:37,719
因此，如果 2 是素元且具有唯一因子分解， 2 就必须整除这两项中的一项，对吧？
Therefore, if 2 were a prime element and we had unique factorization,   2 would have to divide one of these two things, right?

138
00:29:37,719 --> 00:29:45,747
在唯一分解整环中，若素元整除 $ab$，则必整除 $a$ 或 $b$。 这是欧几里得辗转相除法的标准推论。
If you have a unique factorization domain and you have a prime that divides $a b$, it divides $a$ or $b$.   That's by the Euclidean algorithm argument.

139
00:29:45,747 --> 00:29:56,468
但 2 既不整除这项也不整除那项， 因为如果我们试图用 2 去除它，会得到 $(1 + \sqrt{d})/2$，这不是代数整数，对吧？
But 2 doesn't divide either this or that,   because if we tried to divide 2 into this, we get $(1 + \sqrt{d})/2$, which is not an algebraic integer, right?

140
00:29:56,468 --> 00:30:04,839
我们知道这类数域中的代数整数仅由整数加整数倍构成。 同样 2 也不整除那一项，因为商不是代数整数。
We know the algebraic integers in this type are just integers plus integers.   And likewise 2 doesn't divide this, because its quotient is not an algebraic integer.

141
00:30:04,839 --> 00:30:14,280
从而我们有一个不可约元整除乘积却不整除任一因子；因此我们不可能拥有唯一分解整环。
So therefore we have an irreducible element dividing a product but dividing neither part; therefore we can't have a unique factorization domain.

142
00:30:14,280 --> 00:30:18,599
“老师，能把最后那部分再说一遍吗？”
"Yeah, can you just say the last part again?"

143
00:30:18,599 --> 00:30:41,268
Atticus，如果 2 能整除 $1 + \sqrt{d}$，我们就会有：$2 \cdot \frac{1 + \sqrt{d}}{2}$。这是唯一能写出的因式，对吧？ 但这个数并不在 $R$ 中，因为它不是代数整数。
If 2 divided $1 + \sqrt{d}$, Atticus, we'd have this: $2 \cdot \frac{1 + \sqrt{d}}{2}$. That's the only way you can write it, right?   But this number is not in $R$, because it's not an algebraic integer.

144
00:30:41,268 --> 00:30:47,039
因式分解必须在环内部进行； 这只是在数域中唯一能写出的形式。
A factorization has to take place inside the ring;   this is the only way it could be written inside the field.

145
00:30:48,760 --> 00:30:59,182
它为什么不是代数整数？因为若计算它的 $\Delta$，它不是整数。 例如，它不满足任何整系数首一多项式。
Why is it not an algebraic integer? Because if you take its $\Delta$, it's not an integer.   For example, it doesn't satisfy a monic polynomial with integer coefficients.

146
00:30:59,182 --> 00:31:08,599
这就是我们上次算出来的结论： 当 $d \equiv 3 \pmod 4$ 时，代数整数全体仅为整数加上整数倍的 $\sqrt{d}$。
That's what we worked out last time:   that the set of algebraic integers when $d \equiv 3 \pmod 4$ was just this: integers plus integers times $\sqrt{d}$.

147
00:31:08,599 --> 00:31:12,359
而这是 $1/2 + 1/2\sqrt{d}$。
This is $1/2 + 1/2\sqrt{d}$.

148
00:31:12,359 --> 00:31:27,560
好的，所以行不通了。 这个论证只对 $d \equiv 3 \pmod 4$ 有效，而事实证明除了高斯数之外，还有许多其他非唯一分解的情形。
Okay, so that's not any good anymore.   Now this argument only works for $d \equiv 3 \pmod 4$, and it turns out there are other cases besides the Gaussian numbers that have non-unique factorization.

149
00:31:27,560 --> 00:31:44,040
甚至有更强的结论：并不是 $R$ 中的每个理想 $I$ 都是主理想，因为若每个理想均为主理想，我们就会得到唯一分解整环。
So even stronger: not every ideal $I$ in $R$ is principal, because if every ideal were principal, we'd have unique factorization domains.

150
00:31:44,040 --> 00:31:54,199
好，但在所有这些环中普遍成立的是：任何理想都可以由 2 个元素生成。
Okay, now it is always the case for all of these rings that every ideal can be generated by 2 elements.

151
00:31:54,199 --> 00:32:17,519
主理想意味着它由 1 个元素的所有倍数生成； 但无论在哪个环中，任何理想都可由 2 个元素生成，尽管并非所有理想$I \subseteq R$ 都是主理想。
Principal means it's all multiples of 1 element;   but no matter what these rings are, any ideal can be generated by 2 elements, although not all ideals $I \subseteq R$ are principal.

152
00:32:19,079 --> 00:32:35,719
那意味着并非每个 $I$ 都由 1 个元素生成，但每个 $I$ 均可由 2 个元素生成。 这在任意环中不成立，但在这些二次环中成立。
That means not every $I$ is all multiples of 1 element, but every $I$ can be generated by 2 elements.   That's not true in an arbitrary ring, but it is true in these rings.

153
00:32:35,719 --> 00:32:48,159
所以尽管它们不总是欧几里得环或主理想整环，但也没那么糟糕。 为什么呢？为什么？
So they're not the worst thing in the world, even though they're not always Euclidean or principal ideal domains.   Why is that? Why?

154
00:32:52,520 --> 00:33:25,840
首先断言：要么 $I = (0)$，此时由 1 个元素（即 0）生成； 要么 $I$ 在环 $R$ 中具有有限指数——换句话说，$R/I$ 是一个有限环。
Well, the first claim is: either $I = (0)$, in which case it's generated by 1 element,   or $I$ has finite index in the ring $R$—in other words, $R/I$ is a finite ring.

155
00:33:30,599 --> 00:33:52,520
好的。证明：若 $\alpha \in I$ 且 $\alpha \ne 0$， 那么 $\alpha$ 的范数 $\alpha\alpha'$（它是某个正整数 $n > 0$）也必落在 $I$ 中。
Okay. Proof: If $\alpha \ne 0$ in $I$,   then the norm of $\alpha$, which is $\alpha \alpha'$, which is some number $n > 0$, is also in $I$.

156
00:33:52,520 --> 00:33:56,193
这与我们对高斯整数所作的论证完全一致。
So it's the same argument we made for the Gaussian integers.

157
00:33:56,193 --> 00:34:06,599
因此主理想 $(n)$，包含在 $I$ 中：一旦有了整数，其所有倍数都在 $R$ 中。
So the principal ideal $(n)$, is contained in $I$: once I have an integer, I have all multiples of that integer in $R$.

158
00:34:06,599 --> 00:34:22,507
并且该主理想的指数是有限的，等于$n^2$；因为若 $R = \mathbb{Z} + \mathbb{Z} \frac{D + \sqrt{D}}{2}$，
And this index is finite and is equal to $n^2$, because if $R = \mathbb{Z} + \mathbb{Z} \frac{D + \sqrt{D}}{2}$,   then this multiple

159
00:34:22,507 --> 00:34:34,132
则其倍数就是 $n\mathbb{Z} + n\mathbb{Z} \frac{D + \sqrt{D}}{2}$，不同的陪集由 $a$ 和 $b$ 模 $n$ 的不同剩余决定。
is just $n\mathbb{Z} + n\mathbb{Z} \frac{D + \sqrt{D}}{2}$, and the different cosets are given by the different residues of $a$ and $b$ mod $n$.

160
00:34:34,132 --> 00:34:42,199
这里共有 $n^2$ 种可能：$a \pmod n$ 有 $n$ 种可能，$b \pmod n$ 有 $n$ 种可能。
And there are $n^2$ possibilities: $n$ possibilities for $a \pmod n$, and $n$ possibilities for $b \pmod n$.

161
00:34:42,199 --> 00:35:04,840
所以该主理想在环中的指数是 $n^2$； 而 $I$ 夹在它与全环之间，因此商环 $R/I$ 是有限的，其阶数小于等于 $n^2$：$R/I$ 的指数小于或等于 $n^2$。
So the index of this principal ideal in the ring is $n^2$,   and $I$ is squeezed between this and this, so the quotient $R/I$ is finite and is of order less than $n^2$: the index of $R/I$ is less than or equal to $n^2$.

162
00:35:04,840 --> 00:35:12,420
好的，这与我们对高斯整数所作的论证相同。 所以它具有有限指数。
Okay, same argument we made for the Gaussian integers.   So it's a finite index.

163
00:35:12,420 --> 00:35:21,240
现在 Artin 喜欢为此画示意图， 事实上几何图形确实极其有用。
Now Artin likes to draw pictures of these,   and in fact pictures are quite useful.

164
00:35:21,240 --> 00:35:31,839
因此我们要画出 $R$ 的图像，并画出 $I$ 的图像。
So we're going to draw a picture of $R$, and we're going to draw a picture of $I$.

165
00:35:33,560 --> 00:36:00,480
我们将 $R$ 画在复平面中，具体画法如下： 首先我们画出元素1，它当然在 $R$ 中； 然后画出作为 $R$ 另一个生成元的复数，即 $(D + \sqrt{D})/2$。
We draw a picture of $R$ inside of the complex numbers, and we draw it like this:   the first thing we draw is the element 1, that's certainly in $R$;   and then we draw the complex number which is the other generator of $R$, namely this $(D + \sqrt{D})/2$.

166
00:36:02,280 --> 00:36:13,879
我把它画在这上面某个地方，标在这里：$(D + \sqrt{D})/2$。 $\sqrt{D}$是一个纯虚数。
So I'll draw that—that's up here somewhere, let's put it up here: $(D + \sqrt{D})/2$.   $\sqrt{D}$ is an imaginary number.

167
00:36:13,879 --> 00:36:27,639
其实不该这么画，但没关系： 我的意思是实部比虚部大得多，所以实际更像这样，但不管怎样：$(D + \sqrt{D})/2$。
Actually that's not the way to draw it, but never mind:   I mean, the real part is much bigger than the imaginary part, so it really looks more like this, but never mind: $(D + \sqrt{D})/2$.

168
00:36:27,639 --> 00:36:55,937
好，现在 $R$ 由 1 的所有整数倍（2, 3, $-1, -2$ 等） 以及该生成元的所有整数倍构成，所以有这些点； 然后取两者的所有整系数线性组合，所以你还会得到这些、这些点。
Okay, now $R$ consists of all integer multiples of this (2, 3, $-1, -2$, etc.),   and all integer multiples of this, so you get this and this and this;   and then you get all integer multiples of this plus all integer multiples of that, so you also get this, this, this, and this.

169
00:36:55,937 --> 00:37:03,639
于是复平面中的这些点构成了所谓的“格点”（点阵），而 $R$ 恰由这些点组成。
So these points in the complex plane form what's called a lattice, and $R$ consists of exactly those points.

170
00:37:03,639 --> 00:37:08,919
我们在高斯整数中见过这种情形，那里得到的是矩形点阵。
So we've seen this for the Gaussian numbers, where you get the rectangular lattice.

171
00:37:08,919 --> 00:37:38,280
另一个优美的情形是 $D = -3$，得到正六角点阵；而且一般而言你会得到复平面的一个在加法与乘法下封闭的子集， 它是复平面中的离散点集，即 $\mathbb{C}$ 中在乘法下封闭的离散子群。
Another nice case is where $D = -3$ and you get the hexagonal lattice; and in general you get some subset of the complex plane which is stable under addition and multiplication,   but a discrete set of points in the complex plane, a discrete subgroup of $\mathbb{C}$ stable under multiplication.

172
00:37:38,280 --> 00:37:59,639
现在该理想由该格点的一个具有有限指数的子群构成：它可能不包含 1，不包含 2，但它包含外面的某个整数（如前所示）， 因为无论理想中有什么非零元，其范数必落在理想中。
Now this ideal consists of a subgroup of this lattice which has finite index: namely, it might not contain 1, it might not contain 2, but it contains some integer out here, as we saw,   because no matter what we have in it, its norm is then in the ideal.

173
00:37:59,639 --> 00:38:11,639
所以它包含该整数的倍数，对吧？ 然后它还包含这些格点的另一些集合，这就构成了理想。因此它也给出了 $\mathbb{C}$ 的一个离散子群。
So it has some multiple of that, right?   And then it has some other collection of these lattice points, and that forms the ideal. So it also gives a discrete subgroup of $\mathbb{C}$.

174
00:38:11,639 --> 00:38:34,040
$I \subseteq R$ 是一个较小的子群， 它在加法下封闭，更重要的是，它在$R$ 中元素的乘法下封闭（是 $R$-模）。
$I \subseteq R$ is a smaller subgroup,   and it is stable under addition, but even better, it's stable under multiplication by elements from $R$.

175
00:38:34,040 --> 00:38:42,440
一般来说你只需验证它在 $R$ 的那一个生成元的乘法下封闭即可，因为它是加法子群。
And in general, all you have to do is check that it's stable under multiplication by this one generator in $R$, because it's a subgroup.

176
00:38:42,440 --> 00:38:53,480
这意味着它在 1 的乘法下显然封闭， 在任何整数的乘法下也封闭，因为乘以 2只是将元素与自身相加。
So that means it's stable under multiplication by 1, obviously,   and stable under multiplication by any integer, because if you multiply by 2 you're just adding a thing to itself.

177
00:38:53,480 --> 00:39:08,773
随后如果你验证了它在该生成元的乘法下封闭，并且在1 的乘法下封闭，那么它在两者的任意整数组合下均封闭，从而在 $R$ 的作用下封闭。 这正是理想的定义！
But then if you check that it's stable under multiplication by this element, and it's stable under multiplication by 1, then it's stable under multiplication by any integer combination, and hence by $R$.   And that's what an ideal is!

178
00:39:08,773 --> 00:39:16,680
所以从几何图像上看，首先画出 $R$ 的格点， 然后画出 $R$ 的一个在乘法下封闭的子群。
So pictorially, first you draw $R$,   and then you draw a subgroup of $R$ which is stable under multiplication.

179
00:39:16,680 --> 00:39:24,560
我来举一个例子。让我画一个例子，免得大家完全摸不着头脑， 之后我们再讨论两个生成元的事情。
So I'll give an example. Let me draw an example of this so that we don't totally freak out,   and then we'll do this two-element business.

180
00:39:26,919 --> 00:39:45,599
如果可以的话，我来给大家画一个很好的例子。 考虑 $D = -3$ 的情形。在那类情形下，你会得到一个非常有趣的格点。
I'll draw a good example for you if I can.   So let's take the case where $D = -3$. So that's the case where you get a very interesting lattice.

181
00:39:47,000 --> 00:39:53,280
它模 4 余 1，所以大写 $D$ 与小写 $d$ 相同（$D = d = -3$）。
So this is congruent to 1 mod 4, so capital $D$ is the same as little $d$.

182
00:39:55,639 --> 00:40:08,720
好的。所以原来的环 $R$ 可以写成 $\mathbb{Z} + \mathbb{Z} \frac{-3 + \sqrt{-3}}{2}$，
All right. So the original $R$ can be written as $\mathbb{Z} + \mathbb{Z} \frac{-3 + \sqrt{-3}}{2}$,

183
00:40:08,720 --> 00:40:22,394
它与 $\mathbb{Z} + \mathbb{Z} \frac{1 + \sqrt{-3}}{2}$ 是同一个加法群， 因为两者相差的只是相差一个整数 2，所以得到相同的群。
and that's the same group as $\mathbb{Z} + \mathbb{Z} \frac{1 + \sqrt{-3}}{2}$,   because this differs from that just by adding 2 to it, so you get the same group.

184
00:40:22,394 --> 00:40:40,040
好的，我们来画出这个格点，然后画一个理想，我们来画一个主理想： 取理想 $I$ 为由 $\sqrt{-3}$ 生成的主理想，即 $\sqrt{-3}$ 的所有倍数。
All right, let's draw this lattice, and then we'll draw an ideal, and we're going to draw the principal ideal:   we're going to take the ideal $I$ as the ideal generated by $\sqrt{-3}$, all multiples of $\sqrt{-3}$.

185
00:40:40,040 --> 00:40:53,639
好的，开始画图：首先画出 1，然后画出另一个生成元，即这个数：这是一个复数，实部为 $1/2$，虚部为 $\sqrt{3}/2$。
All right, so here we go: the first thing is we have to draw 1, then we have to draw the other generator, which is this: this is a complex number which has real part $1/2$ and imaginary part $\sqrt{3}/2$.

186
00:40:53,639 --> 00:41:04,919
从初等三角学可知它落在单位圆上； 它在上面这里：绕单位圆转过六分之一周（$60^\circ$）。
And it turns out to lie on the unit circle, as you know from basic trigonometry;   and it's up here: it's 1/6 of the way around the unit circle.

187
00:41:04,919 --> 00:41:09,209
这就是 $(1 + \sqrt{-3})/2$。
That's $(1 + \sqrt{-3})/2$.

188
00:41:09,209 --> 00:41:16,600
它的复绝对值等于 1，因为计算它的绝对值，得到 $(1 + 3)/4 = 1$。
So it's a number of complex absolute value 1, because if you take its absolute value, you get $(1 + 3)/4 = 1$.

189
00:41:16,600 --> 00:41:22,919
其实部为 $1/2$，所以正落在那一点。 这是一个 $30^\circ\text{-}60^\circ\text{-}90^\circ$ 的直角三角形。
Its real part is $1/2$, so it lies right there.   This is a $30^\circ\text{-}60^\circ\text{-}90^\circ$ right triangle.

190
00:41:22,919 --> 00:41:50,742
好的。现在画出其他元素：如果用它减去 1，得到这个数； 然后还有 $-1$；然后有这个数的相反数；再有那个数的相反数。 这就是环中绝对值为 1 的 6 个点：即环中的 6 个单位元。
Okay. And now let's draw all the others: if I take this minus 1, I get this number;   then I also have $-1$; then I have minus this number; then I have minus that number.   And those are the 6 points in this ring which have absolute value 1: namely, those are the 6 units of the ring.

191
00:41:50,742 --> 00:41:56,200
好，那么环中有没有绝对值为 $\sqrt{2}$ 的元素呢？
Okay, now do we have anything which has absolute value $\sqrt{2}$?

192
00:41:56,200 --> 00:41:58,079
这些是绝对值为 1 的元素。
So these are things of absolute value 1.

193
00:41:58,079 --> 00:42:07,612
然后我们可以看——环中当然含有 2，但它的范数是 4，对吧？
So then we can go to the— now here we certainly have 2 in it, but that thing has norm 4, right?

194
00:42:07,612 --> 00:42:18,360
接下来的问题是：我们能否在半径为 $\sqrt{2}$ 的圆上找到元素？ 我们能找到 $\Delta(\alpha) = 2$ 的解吗？
The next question is: could we get anything on the circle where the radius of the circle is $\sqrt{2}$?   Do we have any solutions of $\Delta(\alpha) = 2$?

195
00:42:18,360 --> 00:42:28,759
这要求 $a^2 + 3b^2 = 2$，其中 $a, b$ 为整数或半整数，对吧？
Well, this would be $a^2 + 3b^2 = 2$, where $a$ and $b$ are integers or half-integers, right?

196
00:42:28,759 --> 00:42:38,600
答案是找不到这样的解，无论 $a, b \in \frac{1}{2}\mathbb{Z} \setminus \mathbb{Z}$ 还是 $a, b \in \mathbb{Z}$。
And the answer is, you can't find such solutions where $a, b \in \frac{1}{2}\mathbb{Z} \setminus \mathbb{Z}$ or $a, b \in \mathbb{Z}$.

197
00:42:38,600 --> 00:42:42,119
因此在半径为 $\sqrt{2}$ 的圆上没有任何格点。
So there are no elements on the circle of radius $\sqrt{2}$.

198
00:42:42,119 --> 00:42:47,359
好的，那么 $\Delta(\alpha) = 3$ 呢？
All right, how about $\Delta(\alpha) = 3$?

199
00:42:52,210 --> 00:42:58,472
你能解出它等于 3 吗？怎么解？ $a = 0$ 且 $b = 1$，没错！
Can you solve this equal to 3? How?   $a = 0$ and $b = 1$, right!

200
00:42:58,472 --> 00:43:03,800
那么这对应的就是元素 $\sqrt{-3}$，其模长约为 1.7，对吧？
So that would be the element $\sqrt{-3}$, which has length $\sqrt{3} \approx 1.7$, right?

201
00:43:03,800 --> 00:43:11,159
我们往上看：将这两点相加，就得到这个元素，即 $\sqrt{-3}$。
So we go up here: when you add these two things, you get this element, which is $\sqrt{-3}$.

202
00:43:11,159 --> 00:43:26,000
这是离原点次近的点。 一旦有了这个点，用单位元乘它不会改变范数，所以只要找到一个范数为 3 的元素，就必然有 6 个范数为 3 的元素；
That's the next closest thing to the origin.   Now once I have this thing, I have all multiples of it by units, which don't change the norm. So once I find one element of norm 3, I must have 6 elements of norm 3;

203
00:43:26,000 --> 00:43:41,821
它们通过乘以上述单位元得到，即每次精确旋转 $60^\circ$。 如果旋转 $60^\circ$，下一个点就在这里——噢，太美了！
and I get them by multiplying by these units, which means by rotating around by exactly $60^\circ$.   So here if I rotate by $60^\circ$, the next thing is here—oh, this is beautiful!

204
00:43:41,821 --> 00:43:47,194
Peter 知道我为什么这么喜欢这个；你们现在还不知道。
Peter knows why I like this so much; you guys don't know yet.

205
00:43:47,194 --> 00:43:56,960
下一个点在这里；再绕着旋转$120^\circ$，你应该在这里得到一个点，对吧？
But the next thing is here; the next thing, when you rotate around by $120^\circ$, you should get something here, right?

206
00:43:58,600 --> 00:44:07,240
然后我们应该得到它的相反数，在这里得到一个点—— 画得稍微远了一点，但没关系，就在那里。
Then we should get the negative of this, and you should get something out here—   a little too far, but okay, right there.

207
00:44:07,240 --> 00:44:18,440
然后在这外面得到一个点，它是这两者的和，接着还会得到元素 2。
And then we should get something out here, which is the sum of this and that, and then you should get the element 2.

208
00:44:18,440 --> 00:44:44,137
这就是点阵中具有该范数的 6 个点（除了我画得不太准）：这个点与那个点高度相同，所以这些点全在一条直线上，那些点也全在一条直线上。 如果画得准确的话，瞧，Peter：这就是$G_2$ 型根系，对吧？
So here are our 6 things in the lattice (except I didn't draw them very well): this thing has the same height as that, so these things are all on a straight line, and these things are all on a straight line.   If you draw them correctly, there you have it, Peter: the root system of type $G_2$, right?

209
00:44:44,137 --> 00:45:07,080
看看我为什么这么喜欢它——我以前画得挺好的。如果你穿过外面的 6 个点画一个六芒星（大卫之星）， 其边刚好切在内层的 6 个点上。
Let's see why I like this so much—I used to be able to do this well. If you draw a Jewish star through the 6 outer points like that,   and the edges touch the 6 inner points.

210
00:45:07,080 --> 00:45:17,455
很漂亮吧？正好庆祝节日！ 好的，这只是范数为 1 和 3 的点。
Nice, huh? Just celebrating the holiday season!   Okay, now this is just the elements of norm 1 and 3.

211
00:45:17,455 --> 00:45:35,480
然而我断言：外圈这 6 个元素全都在该理想中，对吧？ 而内圈这 6 个元素不在该理想中，因为我们看到那 6 个元素是 $\sqrt{-3}$ 乘上单位元。
However, I claim that these 6 elements out here are all in this ideal, right?   Whereas these 6 inner elements are not in that ideal, because we've seen that these 6 elements are $\sqrt{-3}$ times units.

212
00:45:35,480 --> 00:45:49,836
事实上，如果你取这个理想，它可以由这里的这个元素与其余任意一个元素生成，因为它们给出了子群的一组基。
And in fact, if you take this ideal, it can be generated by this element here and any of the others, because they give a basis for the subgroup.

213
00:45:49,836 --> 00:46:16,960
一般而言——这也是我希望大家直接接受以完成该定理证明的—— $R$ 的任何有限指数子群作为群都可以由 2 个元素生成（暂时抛开它是理想这一事实）。
And in general—and this is something I'm just going to ask you to accept to prove this theorem—   any subgroup of $R$ of finite index can be generated as a subgroup (forget about the fact that it's an ideal) by 2 elements.

214
00:46:16,960 --> 00:46:23,159
这是关于复数中离散子群的一个事实：它们要么由 1 个元素生成，要么由 2 个元素生成。
It's a fact about discrete subgroups of the complex numbers: they're either generated by 1 or 2 elements.

215
00:46:23,159 --> 00:46:29,118
我们在讲刚体运动群的子群时不是证明过吗？
In fact, didn't we prove that when we were doing subgroups of the group of motions?

216
00:46:29,118 --> 00:46:42,702
如果取平面，并且取平移变换的离散子群，它要么为 0，要么由 1 个元素生成，要么由 2 个元素生成。 谢天谢地我们学过刚体运动的离散群！
If you took the plane, and you had a discrete subgroup of translations, right, it was either zero, or generated by 1 element, or generated by 2 elements.   Thank God we did discrete groups of motions!

217
00:46:42,702 --> 00:46:54,340
不管这东西是什么，它首先是子群——先不管乘法封闭性： 它是离散子群；复数无论还有什么结构，先不管乘法，在几何上构成一个平面。
Whatever this thing is, it's a subgroup—forget that it's stable under multiplication:   it's a subgroup, it's discrete; the complex numbers, whatever else they are, forget about their multiplication, form a plane.

218
00:46:54,340 --> 00:46:58,840
因此这个离散子群至多由 2 个元素生成。
So this discrete subgroup is generated by at most 2 elements.

219
00:46:58,840 --> 00:47:06,829
这就是子群的 2 个生成元，先不管它们在乘法下封闭。
So here are the 2 generators of the subgroup, forget that they are stable under multiplication.

220
00:47:06,829 --> 00:47:19,567
这就是为什么，正因为它是一个子群，你就可以用 2 个元素生成它：例如我们当然可以用这个和那个来生成它。 大家可以想象用计算机在一大张纸上打印出这个格点的所有元素。
So that's why, since it's a subgroup, you can generate it by 2 elements: so we can certainly generate it by this, for example, and that.   Well, you can imagine having a computer print out on a big piece of paper all the elements of this lattice.

221
00:47:19,567 --> 00:47:45,879
这是一个格外优美的点阵： 如果以该格点上的所有点为球心、半径取 $1/2$作互不相交的球（圆盘），我画得不太好，但就是这样：以格点为球心， 并且取球的半径为 $1/2$，使得球互不重叠。
This is a particularly beautiful lattice:   if you put spheres of radius $1/2$ centered at the points in this lattice, I'm not doing it very well, but there they are: you take the centers of the spheres to be the points of the lattice,   and you take the radius of the spheres to be $1/2$, so the spheres don't intersect.

222
00:47:45,879 --> 00:47:53,240
那么你就得到了平面上已知的最佳球堆积；事实上已证明这是平面上最紧密的球堆积，称为六角密堆积。
Then you get the best packing we know of spheres in the plane; in fact, it's known to be the best packing of spheres in the plane, called the hexagonal packing.

223
00:47:53,240 --> 00:48:04,695
原因是每个球周围恰好紧挨着 6 个球；这虽然没有覆盖平面的全部面积，但覆盖了将近 90% 的面积。
The reason is, around each sphere you have exactly 6 spheres; and this doesn't cover all the space of the plane, but it covers close to 90% of the area of the plane.

224
00:48:04,695 --> 00:48:20,720
这是二维空间中最密球堆积，而且数十亿年前就被蜜蜂发现了，对吧？
And this is the best sphere packing in dimension 2, and was discovered a billion years ago by the bees, right?

225
00:48:20,720 --> 00:48:28,668
蜜蜂在蜂巢里储存蜂蜜就是这样堆放的：如果你想做圆形储藏并储存尽可能多的蜂蜜。
That's the way you pack honey in a beehive: if you want to make circular packings and you want to store as much honey as possible.

226
00:48:28,668 --> 00:48:36,359
大自然在解决极值问题方面具有惊人的智慧，而且大自然解决这个问题比数学家早了无数年。
So nature has an amazing way of solving extremal problems, and nature has solved this problem many, many years before the mathematicians got to it.

227
00:48:36,359 --> 00:48:51,320
你们会很高兴听到：Noam Elkies 教授与他的一位杰出研究生（现任职于微软研究院）最近证明了 8 维和 24 维的最优球堆积。 我们过去就知道候选点阵，但他们终于给出了严格证明！
You'll be happy to hear that Professor Elkies, working with one of his distinguished graduate students who's now at Microsoft, has found the best packings of spheres in dimensions 8 and 24 recently.   We knew what they were, but they've been able to prove it!

228
00:48:51,320 --> 00:48:54,680
现在我们可没有生活在 24 维的蜜蜂。
Now we don't have any bees that are working in dimension 24.

229
00:48:54,680 --> 00:49:11,564
然而，过去常常是——我特别喜欢这个掌故——当数学家谈论 8 维、12 维或 24 维（24 对数学家来说是一个绝对神奇的维度！）的某种现象时，做硬科学的人就会嘲笑他们，笑着说：
However, you know, it used to be—I just love this—it used to be the fact that when mathematicians would talk about some phenomenon in dimension 8, or dimension 12, or dimension 24 (24 happens to be an absolutely magical dimension for mathematicians!), they'd talk about this,

230
00:49:11,564 --> 00:49:28,332
“得了吧，你们根本教不了我们什么，因为在二维我们几十亿年前就知道了，在三维我们也早就知道了， 你们数学家连个球堆积都证不出来，而且我们根本不在乎三维以上的空间，对吧？”
and the people doing hard science would laugh, and they'd say,   "Well, you can't tell us anything, because in 2 dimensions we've known this for billions of years, and in 3 dimensions we've known it for millions of years,   and you can't even do anything, and we don't care about more than 3 dimensions, right?"

231
00:49:28,332 --> 00:49:43,322
好吧，现在如果你直接走到杰斐逊物理实验室：现在一半的物理学家都在讨论 10 维和 11 维发生的事情， 因为只有在那些维度他们才能化解物理学中的微分方程！
Okay, now if you just go over to Jefferson: now half the people are talking about what happens in dimension 10 and dimension 11,   because those are the only dimensions where they can resolve the differential equations of physics!

232
00:49:43,322 --> 00:49:57,399
现在人们认为我们生活在一个 10 维宇宙中，其中我们能看到 4 维（3 维空间，1 维时间），还有 6 个蜷缩在 6 维紧致流形中的微小维度， 尺度大约相当于普朗克尺度。
So now it's believed that we live in a 10-dimensional universe, of which we see 4 dimensions (three of space, one of time), and there are 6 tiny little dimensions all in a little manifold of dimension 6,   about the same size as Planck's constant.

233
00:49:57,399 --> 00:50:09,639
所以我们永远看不到它，但它具有极其重要的几何形状，称为卡拉比-丘流形（Calabi-Yau manifold）， 以我们哈佛的丘成桐教授命名；这种几何形状化解了宇宙物理微分方程的所有困难！
So we'll never see it, but it has a very important shape called the Calabi-Yau manifold,   named after Professor Yau here; and that shape resolves all all the difficulties of differential equations in the universe!

234
00:50:09,639 --> 00:50:18,937
所以我特别喜欢这个反转：突然之间，物理学家开始热衷于24 维：“能跟我们多讲讲 26 维吗？” 每一个维度都有其独特魅力。
So I just love the fact that all at once, you know, they're really into what happens in dimension 24: "Can you tell us more about dimension 26?"   Each one of these dimensions has its own charm.

235
00:50:18,937 --> 00:50:32,412
但回到我们的主题，在二维中：我们发现理想不一定由 1 个元素生成——我们证明了有大量不是 PID 的情形—— 但它们均可由 2 个元素生成。
But here's what happens in dimension 2: we find that ideals are generated not necessarily by 1 element—we've shown that there are plenty of cases that aren't PIDs—   but they're generated by 2 elements.

236
00:50:32,412 --> 00:50:54,280
周五，Peter 将向大家展示如何在这些环中挽救唯一因子分解，因为那是19 世纪中叶数学家们的一项重大发现： 当时发现元素无法总是分解为素元（我们刚才看到了例子），但你可以把理想分解为素理想的乘积！
Now on Friday, Peter is going to show you how you rescue unique factorization in these rings, because that was a huge discovery in the middle of the 19th century by mathematicians:   it was discovered that you couldn't always factor an element into primes (we've seen examples of that), but you could factor ideals into prime ideals!

237
00:50:54,280 --> 00:51:12,379
也就是说，理想之间定义了乘法运算；随后有了素元向理想的推广——称为“素理想”； 并且每个理想都能唯一分解为素理想的乘积。这是一个极其重大的成果！
Namely, there was a generalization of multiplication for ideals; then there was a generalization of irreducible elements that took place for ideals, called prime ideals;   and that every ideal could be written uniquely as a product of prime ideals. That's a huge result!

238
00:51:12,379 --> 00:51:31,148
接着Peter 还会告诉大家如何度量这类环距离唯一分解整环有多远（理想类群与类数）； 这正是我深入研究过很多的内容，我会在下周一跟大家讲。好的，周一见！
And then Peter will also show you how you measure how far one of these rings is away from being a unique factorization domain;   and that's something I've worked on a lot, and I'll talk to you about that on Monday. Okay, see you then!
